    "content": "## The Myth of Required Industry Experience\n\nRecruiters and hiring committees frequently publish job descriptions stating '15+ years of direct industry experience required.' In practice, forward-thinking boards frequently hire senior leaders from outside their vertical when their sector faces stagnation or systemic disruption.\n\nConsider the historical precedents: retail banking hiring e-commerce executives to reinvent digital consumer lending; hospital systems recruiting hospitality leaders to improve patient satisfaction scores; automotive manufacturing hiring aerospace executives to drive automated battery assembly.\n\n## Finding the High-Probability Pivot Corridor\n\nCross-industry pivots are rarely random; they succeed when your native industry solved a problem that your target industry is currently struggling with:\n- **FMCG to Digital Health**: Consumer goods leaders understand brand loyalty, unit packaging economics, and direct consumer engagement—skills digital therapeutics desperately lack.\n- **Telecom to Utilities/Smart Grid**: Managing distributed physical infrastructure and billing millions of recurring subscribers translates directly into modern renewable energy grids.\n- **Automotive to Medical Device Manufacturing**: Automotive leaders bring world-class Six Sigma tolerances, supplier audits, and cost containment to medical device assembly lines.\n\n## How to Pitch Universal Commercial Competence\n\nIn executive search interviews, deliberately strip your vocabulary of internal company acronyms. Speak strictly in universal commercial metrics:\n- 'We improved Gross Margin by 420 basis points through automated supplier bidding.'\n- 'We reduced customer onboarding cycle times from 21 days to 48 hours while maintaining 99.8% compliance.'\n- 'We grew employee retention from 81% to 94% across 8 distributed regional fulfillment hubs.'\n\nWhen asked about your lack of vertical history, state clearly: 'Your internal team already has deep domain knowledge. What I bring is a proven operational framework from an industry that already solved this bottleneck at 5x higher scale.'"
