    "content": "## Moving from Candidate to Due Diligence Partner\n\nWhen interviewing for director, VP, or C-level positions, the dynamic changes from a job interview to a strategic transaction. If you join an organization with hidden accounting irregularities, unaligned board factions, or an unsustainable burn rate, your personal professional brand will bear the reputational cost.\n\nWhen the hiring panel asks 'What questions do you have for us?', asking generic questions like 'What is a typical day like?' is disqualifying. You must ask probing diagnostic questions that reveal the underlying reality of the balance sheet and board dynamics.\n\n## The 10 High-Signal Executive Diagnostic Inquiries\n\n1. **Board Alignment on Strategic Risk**: 'How aligned is the Board on the single greatest operational risk facing this organization over the next 24 months, and where does disagreement exist?'\n2. **The Forensic Reason for the Opening**: 'What did my predecessor do exceptionally well, and where did the Board or executive committee feel strategic velocity stalled?'\n3. **Discretionary Capital Realities**: 'What is the approved capital expenditure budget for this division over the next fiscal year, and what hurdles exist for unbudgeted investments?'\n4. **Cultural Conflict Resolution**: 'When was the last time the executive leadership team fundamentally disagreed on a major strategic decision, and how was consensus finally forged?'\n5. **Customer Retention Vulnerabilities**: 'Which enterprise customer or contract represents our greatest revenue concentration risk, and what is our net revenue retention trajectory?'\n6. **Autonomy vs. Governance**: 'Where does my operational decision-making authority end and Board approval begin on personnel changes, vendor contracts, and pricing?'\n7. **Underperforming Unit History**: 'How long has the underperforming unit been struggling, and what previous intervention strategies were attempted and abandoned?'\n8. **Employee Attrition Drivers**: 'What does voluntary exit interview data from top-decile performers reveal about our organizational culture?'\n9. **Debt & Refinancing Covenants**: 'What debt maturity milestones or covenant obligations are coming due within the next 36 months?'\n10. **The 1-Year Success Definition**: 'If we sit down together 12 months from today, what exact numbers must be on the scorecard for you to say this hire was a home run?'"
